": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Listen to the audio. Type in the missing words."}]}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 11, "type": "RSLT", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}], "template_override": 1}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn7le18ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le18ob04re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn7le18ob04re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Let's go along here. I want to get a rice cooker.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Wow. I've never tried one out.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I was thinking I could use it to whip up rice dishes quickly and efficiently.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Like what?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I have a recipe for squid that's chopped up, then mixed with herbed fried rice that looks delicious!", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn7le18ob04re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Squid makes me squeamish. Don't they squirt black ink?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: There's a little sac of it inside them that you squeeze out. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Ick! Squishy seafood!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: OK. Would squab stuffed with wild rice, cranberries and nuts be better for you?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I think so. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Acorn squash hollowed out and filled with zucchini and rice is also a nice staple.", "id": 2, "time": "20000", "image": "engenn7le18ob04re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: What are we going to do after the cook-in?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Could we listen to music and talk?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Marleene might leave early. Could we go out for coffee and see a movie or do a little window shopping?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Could walk along the Charles River starting at Kendal Square and then listen to the buskers along the esplanade? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Could end up coming back for some more of your green tea cake?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sounds like we've come up with some good ideas!", "id": 3, "time": "40000", "image": "engenn7le18ob04re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}, {"id": 2, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Rice Cookout"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Cooking Up a Storm"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Pronunciation of Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Where do you put the stress in a phrasal verb?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the phrasal verb needs an object, or is not separable, then you stress the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">taken</span> with</span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">go</span> along</span><br/><span class=\"italic\">How long have you been <span class=\"strong\">taken</span> with food and cooking?</span> (taken with - is not finished without the objects food and cooking)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Let's <span class=\"strong\">go</span> along here.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the phrasal verb is separable, then the stress is on the particle (preposition)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <span class=\"italic\">whip <span class=\"strong\">up</span></span><br/><span class=\"italic\">I'll whip <span class=\"strong\">up</span> a rice dish. <br/>I'll whip a rice dish <span class=\"strong\">up</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Let's <span class=\"strong\">go</span> along here."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've <span class=\"strong\">been</span> into cooking in a big way."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've been <span class=\"strong\">reading</span> up on the different types of rice."}, {"type": "example", "content": "How long have you been <span class=\"strong\">taken</span> with food and cooking?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've never tried one <span class=\"strong\">out</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I could use it to whip <span class=\"strong\">up</span> rice dishes quickly and efficiently."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have a recipe for squid that's chopped <span class=\"strong\">up</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Acorn squash hollowed <span class=\"strong\">out</span> and filled with zucchini and rice is a nice staple."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Pronouncing the Letters  <span class=\"italic\">squ</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When two or more consonants appear together and you hear each sound that each consonant would normally make, the consonant team is called a <span class=\"strong\">consonant blend</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In words with <span class=\"italic\">squ</span>, you blend the <span class=\"strong\">s</span> sound and the <span class=\"strong\">qu</span> (kw) to make the <span class=\"strong\">squ</span> (skw) sound as in <span class=\"italic\">squid</span> and <span class=\"italic\">squelch</span>. Note that <span class=\"strong\">sq</span> is always followed by <span class=\"strong\">u</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say these words out loud. Notice the blending of the sounds /s/ and /kw/."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squid\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skwid)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"square\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skware)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squirt\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skwirt)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squab\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skwab)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squishy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skwishy)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squeamish\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skweemish)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squeeze\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skweez)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squash\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skwash)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now try saying these sentences out loud."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Squishy seafood!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Squid makes me squeamish.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Don't they squirt black ink?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have a recipe for squid that's chopped up.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could walk along the Charles starting at Kendal Square.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to whip up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make quickly and easily"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's whip up a nice dessert."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when talk about cooking squid."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "squid"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a sea animal with a long body"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a recipe for squid."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to chop up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cut into pieces"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Please chop up the vegetables."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to mix with"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to combine"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The vegetables mixed with fried rice looks delicious!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "squeamish"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling upset or nauseated by something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Squid makes me squeamish! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "squab"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a young pigeon"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You'd like squab stuffed with wild rice better."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hollow out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take out what is inside"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Acorn squash hollowed out and filled with zucchini and rice is a nice staple."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to squeeze"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to press something out"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You squeeze the ink out of that small sac."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob04aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "squishy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "soft and wet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Ick! Squishy seafood!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob04aud09"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le18ob04re1img01.jpg "}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Invent a tongue twister using the <span class=\"italic\">SQU</span> sound. (For example, a P sound tongue twister: <span class=\"italic\">Peter piper picked a peck of pickled peppers</span>)"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Write down the tongue twister."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice the tongue twister by saying it 3 times in a row slowly."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Try the tongue twister many times more quickly."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a tongue twister using <span class=\"italic\">SQU</span> sounds."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice the <span class=\"italic\">SQU</span> sound slowly."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice the <span class=\"italic\">SQU</span> sound more quickly."}]}], "type": "sena"}